meta {
  name: List connector types
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/connectors/types
}

docs {
  The catalog of connector types and each type's configurable fields (which are required,
  which are secrets), plus each type's supported `modes`. Use this to fill `options` for the
  connector you create next.

  A type may also carry `next_step` — what you must do AFTER saving, for connectors that
  aren't usable the moment they're created (OneDrive needs an interactive Microsoft 365
  sign-in, which can only happen once the connector exists).

  Each field carries `multiline` — true for prose fields a UI should render as a textarea
  rather than a single-line input. Every type has one: `extraction_prompt`, an optional
  description of what this source's documents contain, which guides knowledge-graph
  extraction for it (needs `graph.extract_triples` on in /api/settings).
}
